From: ThirdReality <dev@3reality.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: MGMT: Fix double list_del in command complete handlers

Stable 6.6.158 backported upstream 302a1f674c00 ("Bluetooth: MGMT: Fix
possible UAFs"), which turned mgmt_pending_valid() into a check that also
unlinks the command from hdev->mgmt_pending.  The completion handlers were
not updated accordingly on the 6.6 branch, so they call
mgmt_pending_remove() (an unconditional list_del) after the command has
already been unlinked.  This corrupts the list and on arm64 ends in:

  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address dead000000000108
  pc : mgmt_pending_remove+0x24/0x64
  lr : mgmt_pending_remove+0x20/0x64
  Call trace:
   mgmt_pending_remove+0x24/0x64
   mgmt_add_adv_patterns_monitor_complete+0x120/0x17c
   hci_cmd_sync_work+0xac/0x150

Fix both handlers the same way upstream did in 17f89341cb42:

  - mgmt_add_adv_patterns_monitor_complete(): use mgmt_pending_free(),
    the command is already unlinked by mgmt_pending_valid().
  - set_mesh_complete(): drop the mgmt_pending_foreach() walk that could
    free unrelated pending mesh commands, send the status with
    mgmt_cmd_status() using cmd->opcode and free the command once in the
    common exit path.

Fixes: 302a1f674c00 ("Bluetooth: MGMT: Fix possible UAFs")
diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
index a678a4a57c..ca7c092ea4 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt.c
@@ -2162,13 +2162,14 @@ static void set_mesh_complete(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data, int err)
 	sk = cmd->sk;
 
 	if (status) {
-		mgmt_pending_foreach(MGMT_OP_SET_MESH_RECEIVER, hdev, true,
-				     cmd_status_rsp, &status);
-		return;
+		mgmt_cmd_status(cmd->sk, hdev->id, cmd->opcode, status);
+		goto done;
 	}
 
-	mgmt_pending_remove(cmd);
 	mgmt_cmd_complete(sk, hdev->id, MGMT_OP_SET_MESH_RECEIVER, 0, NULL, 0);
+
+done:
+	mgmt_pending_free(cmd);
 }
 
 static int set_mesh_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data)
@@ -5426,7 +5427,7 @@ static void mgmt_add_adv_patterns_monitor_complete(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 
 	mgmt_cmd_complete(cmd->sk, cmd->hdev->id, cmd->opcode,
 			  mgmt_status(status), &rp, sizeof(rp));
-	mgmt_pending_remove(cmd);
+	mgmt_pending_free(cmd);
 
 	hci_dev_unlock(hdev);
 	bt_dev_dbg(hdev, "add monitor %d complete, status %d",
